// Both fixes AS AGENTCORE NEEDS THEM: every policy scoped to the gateway, and `eventResource:
// resource` in every predicate, which AgentCore's temporal policy examples make mandatory.
//
// THIS FILE IS NOT CHECKED BY ANCHOR, which does not yet model AgentCore's event schema and refuses
// both constructs (see ../../../../src/Anchor.MCPServer/knowledge/the-modelled-subset.md). What IS
// checked is ../agent-policy.dw and ../07-trust-decay.dw: the same rules with the scope and the
// joins removed, which changes nothing when every request goes through one gateway. This file is
// that checked text with the two put back, and it parses with `dogwood check-parse`. `<gateway ARN>`
// is the article's own placeholder.

// ---- the trade gate: output-to-input integrity AND data freshness, in one rule ---------------
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<gateway ARN>"
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 24h AgentCore::Action::"get_client_profile"::response{
        eventResource: resource,
        input.profile_id: context.input.profile_id
    }
    && formerly within 30s AgentCore::Action::"get_market_price"::response{
        eventResource: resource
    }
};

// ---- trust decay: `when`, not `unless` --------------------------------------------------------
// AS A STANDALONE POLICY, which is how the article publishes it, and what TrustDecay.tla checks.
// Deployed BESIDE the trade gate above it would be a second permit on execute_trade, so either
// rule would allow a trade -- the same alternatives effect as finding 2. In a set, "loses access"
// is a restriction, and a restriction composes as a forbid:
//
//     forbid (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade", resource == ...)
//     unless temporal {
//         formerly within 15m AgentCore::Action::"interact_advisor"::response{ eventResource: resource }
//     };
//
// That forbid form is NOT machine-checked here: TradeGate.tla's sessions have no advisor event, so
// it would need a module stating all three protections together.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<gateway ARN>"
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 15m AgentCore::Action::"interact_advisor"::response{
        eventResource: resource
    }
};

// The prerequisites each needs permitted, so that they are recorded as `response` events.
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"get_client_profile", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<gateway ARN>");
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"get_market_price", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<gateway ARN>");
permit (principal, action == AgentCore::Action::"interact_advisor", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"<gateway ARN>");
